[b]Hand those pesky logistics chores to your steward.
Ride into a town or village and one glanceable table shows what the party needs — nudge any row, then one click: Do it.[/b]

[h1]Looking for…?[/h1]

If one of these searches brought you here — yes, this is that mod:
[list]
[*]a mod to [b]auto buy food[/b] — enough of it, and [b]varied[/b] for morale
[*]a mod to [b]buy horses for your infantry[/b] — faster on the campaign map
[*]a mod to [b]keep a set number of war horses[/b] for your cavalry upgrades
[*]a mod to [b]sell loot in bulk[/b] — all the weapons and armour, one click
[*]a mod to [b]auto ransom prisoners[/b]
[*]a mod to [b]hire companions without the dialogue[/b]
[/list]

[h1]What your steward does[/h1]

[list]
[*][b]Tavern[/b] — the wanderers for hire and the tavern's mercenaries, each hired with a click. Never suggested: you choose. Names in gold open the Encyclopedia
[*][b]Troops[/b] — the recruits the notables offer you here (towns and villages), then your own troops: recruit or dismiss with a click, past the party limit if you like — the footer shows it. Food and horses follow your new party at once
[*][b]Food[/b] — keeps enough for everyone (40 days of it by default, at your party's own rate — prisoners eat half), buys the kinds you have least of first for variety, sells real surplus
[*][b]Horses[/b] — keeps your pack animals (10 by default) and a horse for every footman (110 per 100), the war horses you choose to keep among them. Cheapest bought, surplus sold dearest first; noble horses sold unless you lock them, lame ones replaced by healthy ones
[*][b]Armour & weapons[/b] — loot sold in groups (armour, melee, ranged, shields): cheapest first, or most kilos per denar to shed the most weight. [i]Off until you tick "Sell loot"[/i]
[*][b]Prisoners[/b] — ransomed in towns (lords only if you say so), or donated for influence to your kingdom's dungeons (not your own clan's)
[*][b]Full-autonomous steward[/b] [i](off by default)[/i] — for when you are rich and done micromanaging: on arrival the steward does it all without the window, never lets the chest drop below 100,000 (by default), never hires from the tavern, and leaves one report line in the message log
[/list]

Money has an order: sell first, then food before horses, and two floors you set — gold you always keep, and gold you keep before buying animals. Food and horses have a price rule too: by default never bought above the average price +20%, never sold below −20%.

[h1]How to use it[/h1]

[list]
[*]Enter a town or village — the [b]Party Steward[/b] opens by itself when there is something to do. Or pick [b]Party Steward[/b] in the town or village menu, right after Trade
[*][b]Suggestion[/b] tab — one row per thing: what you have, the change, the result, the price, the market's stock. The header shows your gold now » after
[*][b][–] [+][/b] on any row: [b]click[/b] ±1, [b]Shift[/b] ±5, [b]Ctrl[/b] all. The round arrow puts a row back to the steward's suggestion; Reset all puts back everything. A greyed button tells you why on hover
[*][b]Do it[/b] — carried out through the game's own trade, ransom and hiring, so Trade XP and quests count as if you did it by hand
[*][b]Prices[/b] tab — your price book: per kind of food and horse, tick buy or sell and type your own price, or leave it empty for the average
[*][b]Instructions[/b] tab — every standing order, grouped, saved at once
[*]Leaving without a look? The steward asks once: [i]Review[/i] or [i]Leave anyway[/i]
[*]Armour and weapons you [b]lock[/b] in the inventory screen are never sold. Locked food and horses are still managed — turn on [i]Locks protect food & horses[/i] to keep those too
[/list]

[h1]Settings[/h1]

[list]
[*]Every number is yours: in the Instructions tab, in [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859238197]Mod Configuration Menu (MCM)[/url] — [b]optional[/b] — or in a plain file with a comment above every key (meaning, default, range):
[i]Documents\Mount and Blade II Bannerlord\Configs\SmartSteward\settings.json[/i]
[*]All three show the same values. Delete the file to go back to defaults
[*]What was planned and done goes to [i]smart_steward.log[/i] beside it — attach it to a bug report
[/list]

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]

[list]
[*]Bannerlord [b]v1.4.8[/b]. [b]War Sails[/b] is fine but not needed (docking at a port brings the steward too, and the leave question guards Set sail)
[*][b]No Harmony[/b] — only vanilla's own actions, so it sits politely beside other mods
[*][b]Save-safe[/b] — nothing is stored in your save: add it or remove it mid-campaign
[*]MCM optional; load it before Smart Steward if you use it (the launcher sorts that)
[/list]

[h1]Known limits[/h1]

[list]
[*]Towns and villages only — castles have no market
[*]Only the market you stand in: no trade routes
[*]Livestock is left alone; lame or old horses are never bought
[*]A row you edit stays as you set it — the steward does not re-balance the others around it
[*]Town prices move as you trade; the steward re-checks every unit at Do it and stops rather than overpay
[*]Trade goods (wood, jewelry, tools…) are not in the price book yet — planned for a later update
[*]English only for now
[/list]

[h1]Translations welcome[/h1]

Every word the mod says is in one file: [i]ModuleData\Languages\std_SmartSteward.xml[/i]. Copy it into [i]Languages\XX[/i], translate the texts — the file's header says how, the vanilla way.

